    "recommendations": "Ensuring the single access point and extended driveway remain clear of obstructions at all times could significantly improve emergency vehicle ingress and egress, particularly given the limited options for rear access. Posting clearly visible address markers at the street frontage and at the driveway entrance would support rapid navigation by responding units. Where pedestrian walkways connect the main building to the detached structure, keeping those pathways unobstructed may assist personnel movement during operations. Confirming that the driveway width and surface condition support large emergency vehicle access could further enhance response effectiveness across the property."
