    "recommendations": "Reducing the density of brush and vegetation in direct contact with or immediately adjacent to the structure would meaningfully improve defensible space and reduce opportunities for fire to transition toward the building. Where shrubs and other vegetation are concentrated near improvements, increasing separation between plant groupings and the structure may reduce fuel continuity and limit the potential for fire spread through connected vegetation. Maintaining the existing open terrain and any natural fuel breaks on the property could support suppression operations and provide firefighters with safer working conditions. Given that the property is served by a single access route, keeping that route clear of encroaching vegetation along its edges would support both firefighter access and evacuation. Continued management of vegetation within the immediate structure perimeter, combined with preserving open areas that interrupt fuel continuity, would support long-term wildfire resilience and improve overall property preparedness."
